 ## Payment flow
 
 When a customer chooses a voucher method for payment, they receive a digital voucher through email or in an app with a transaction summary and a voucher code. The customer scans the voucher code at an authorized location like a convenience store and pays in-person, often with cash.
-![Figure describing the four step voucher payment flow. First, customer selects voucher payment at checkout. Next, they receive a voucher with transaction reference. Then, they provide voucher and cash at a store, ATM, or bank. Finally, receive notification that payment is complete.](assets/stripe-vouchers-payment-flow.svg)
+![Figure describing the four step voucher payment flow. First, customer selects voucher payment at checkout. Next, they receive a voucher with transaction reference. Then, they provide voucher and cash at a store, ATM, or bank. Finally, receive notification that payment is complete.](https://b.stripecdn.com/docs-statics-srv/assets/payment_flow.3f6e339397147be5fa542edec11d7060.svg)
 
